1
00:00:01,768 --> 00:00:02,669
EPISODE 9

2
00:00:02,736 --> 00:00:03,971
Our Hwa-ran blossomed!

3
00:00:04,037 --> 00:00:06,673
How could she look so…

4
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:09,276
I'm amazed by how much she's changed.

5
00:00:10,043 --> 00:00:11,345
Thank you.

6
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:15,349
By the way, how old are you?

7
00:00:17,651 --> 00:00:20,187
What? Why does my heart keep racing?

8
00:00:20,254 --> 00:00:22,422
Could I really be falling for Hwa-ran?

9
00:00:22,489 --> 00:00:24,391
No, that's impossible. No way.

10
00:00:24,458 --> 00:00:26,760
I admit she's prettier than I thought.

11
00:00:26,827 --> 00:00:27,995
But with Hwa-ran,

12
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:30,330
nothing's changed. I'm not interested.

13
00:00:30,397 --> 00:00:32,900
Then why is my heart pounding? Why?

14
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,571
That's it! It's that kind of feeling.

15
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:45,479
Ma'am, when will my food be ready?

16
00:00:45,546 --> 00:00:47,214
Just wait a moment.

17
00:00:48,815 --> 00:00:51,218
I never noticed
the snack shop part-timer

18
00:00:51,285 --> 00:00:52,853
when she was in the kitchen…

19
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,821
-Done for the day?
-Yes.

20
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:56,557
Get home safe.

21
00:00:58,992 --> 00:01:00,928
As she went home in a miniskirt,

22
00:01:00,994 --> 00:01:03,897
call it amazement at running into her?

23
00:01:06,166 --> 00:01:10,103
Right, being that amazed
can make your heart race, too.

24
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:11,738
I'm sure of it.

25
00:01:17,844 --> 00:01:19,079
-Han-cheol!
-Hey!

26
00:01:19,146 --> 00:01:21,114
-What happened?
-Hey, what's wrong?

27
00:01:21,181 --> 00:01:23,617
Hey, hey, what's wrong with you?

28
00:01:23,684 --> 00:01:26,353
-Hey, he's bleeding!
-What's wrong? Hey, wake up!

29
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:28,121
Hey, Yoo Han-cheol! Han-cheol!

30
00:01:28,188 --> 00:01:29,856
Oh no, what's wrong with him?

31
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:31,458
Who beat him? He's drooling.

32
00:01:32,659 --> 00:01:34,394
What? You're dating Su-yeon?

33
00:01:34,461 --> 00:01:38,231
Yes, yes! That's right, you punks.

34
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:40,901
Wow, you actually pulled it off.

35
00:01:40,968 --> 00:01:42,502
Way to go, Yoo Han-cheol.

36
00:01:42,569 --> 00:01:45,672
It's all thanks to you guys.

37
00:01:45,739 --> 00:01:48,642
So everyone's in a couple
except me and Hyeok?

38
00:01:51,345 --> 00:01:54,281
-Hey, it's back!
-It's back! Get ready!

39
00:01:54,348 --> 00:01:56,316
-Do we have to now?
-Yes, right now.

40
00:01:57,484 --> 00:02:00,621
Seriously, what are we doing? Play!

41
00:02:00,687 --> 00:02:03,290
-Here we go!
-What are we doing, damn it?

42
00:02:19,172 --> 00:02:21,942
Hey, water deer! Go away already!

43
00:02:23,610 --> 00:02:27,114
Big bro's in a good mood today, so go!

44
00:02:29,850 --> 00:02:31,985
Hey, do we have to do this every day?

45
00:02:32,052 --> 00:02:34,688
-I don't know.
-Why won't it leave?

46
00:02:39,693 --> 00:02:43,096
Wow, you guys are awesome!

47
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:44,264
Seriously amazing!

48
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:48,001
Hey, what are you doing here again?

49
00:02:48,568 --> 00:02:50,437
I didn't come here to see you.

50
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:53,907
Sir.

51
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:59,012
You're so cool, handsome!
Is there anything you can't do?

52
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:03,050
But if you're this good,
why didn't you ever debut?

53
00:03:03,116 --> 00:03:06,353
Because some pretty boy
you adore so much

54
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:08,422
caused trouble and ruined it…

55
00:03:08,488 --> 00:03:11,258
Did this guy break?
Why does it sound so weird?

56
00:03:11,324 --> 00:03:13,026
Oh, I see.

57
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:19,132
Excuse me, guys.
Then should I be your Manager?

58
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,934
-Manager?
-Yes.

59
00:03:21,001 --> 00:03:24,071
I may not look it, but I have
over 1,000 regular viewers

60
00:03:24,137 --> 00:03:26,473
as an online live streamer.

61
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,809
I can promote you guys big-time.

62
00:03:29,676 --> 00:03:30,911
Do whatever you want.

63
00:03:30,977 --> 00:03:33,780
Okay! Then starting right now,

64
00:03:33,847 --> 00:03:36,850
I'm the Manager of Excellent Souls!

65
00:03:45,292 --> 00:03:48,395
I did all the laundry before I left!

66
00:03:51,598 --> 00:03:53,066
Why curse at these guys?

67
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:55,736
I told you, they're not bad people!

68
00:04:01,475 --> 00:04:04,711
Wow, she sure has a tough life.

69
00:04:04,778 --> 00:04:07,647
But what was that man even saying?

70
00:04:07,714 --> 00:04:09,416
Hey, you know what…

71
00:04:10,717 --> 00:04:12,886
I kind of know what that man said.

72
00:04:12,953 --> 00:04:15,956
-Really?
-Then what did he say at the end?

73
00:04:19,392 --> 00:04:22,562
What? Why would he insult our parents?

74
00:04:22,629 --> 00:04:25,899
He crossed the line.
He should raise his daughter better.

75
00:04:25,966 --> 00:04:28,902
Hey, hasn't that man
gotten even worse toward us?

76
00:04:28,969 --> 00:04:30,570
What? He's always hated us.

77
00:04:30,637 --> 00:04:32,773
He's hated us since we stole apples.

78
00:04:32,839 --> 00:04:36,176
No, he's definitely gotten even worse.

79
00:04:36,243 --> 00:04:38,078
Oh, come on! It's back again!

80
00:04:38,145 --> 00:04:40,614
-Hey, everyone get ready!
-Hurry up, let's go!

81
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:06,740
What are you doing out here?
Have you all lost your minds?

82
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:10,544
Since you're talking so roughly,
you must be feeling better, sir.

83
00:05:10,610 --> 00:05:15,015
Thanks to you boys,
I caught the thief and got my ginseng.

84
00:05:15,081 --> 00:05:16,716
But what are you doing here?

85
00:05:16,783 --> 00:05:18,351
Well, the truth is…

86
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:22,289
a water deer ate our seedlings.

87
00:05:22,355 --> 00:05:23,857
We've been at this for days.

88
00:05:23,924 --> 00:05:27,327
You bunch of idiots!
All this over a measly water deer?

89
00:05:27,394 --> 00:05:31,031
It's fine, it's fine. Leave it to me.

90
00:05:56,156 --> 00:05:57,791
All done!

91
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:00,827
Stick this in the ground,
and the water deer's done for.

92
00:06:00,894 --> 00:06:02,696
-Bye-bye, y'all!
-What is this?

93
00:06:02,762 --> 00:06:07,234
This is called cresol soap solution.

94
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:10,403
Wild animals really hate this smell.

95
00:06:10,470 --> 00:06:13,940
Wild animals come down looking
for something to eat,

96
00:06:14,007 --> 00:06:16,176
and one whiff makes them go, "Mommy!"

97
00:06:16,243 --> 00:06:18,111
"What is that, fermented skate?"

98
00:06:18,178 --> 00:06:21,648
"Gosh, my nose is rotting!"
And they'll bolt at full speed.

99
00:06:22,315 --> 00:06:25,919
Then we don't need to struggle
standing guard out here anymore.

100
00:06:25,986 --> 00:06:27,287
Of course not, my boy.

101
00:06:27,354 --> 00:06:30,056
Forget water deer,
even Godzilla can't get in now!

102
00:06:30,123 --> 00:06:32,626
You really are the true Farming God.

103
00:06:32,692 --> 00:06:35,795
Oh, come on, it's nothing special.

104
00:06:35,862 --> 00:06:39,232
We went through all that
not knowing it was this simple? Jeez!

105
00:06:39,299 --> 00:06:41,301
Tell me about it.

106
00:06:41,368 --> 00:06:42,569
Let's get going.

107
00:06:42,636 --> 00:06:46,640
I'm cold, hungry, and out of energy.

108
00:06:46,706 --> 00:06:49,075
Are you running low on energy?

109
00:06:49,142 --> 00:06:51,044
-Yes.
-All right!

110
00:06:51,111 --> 00:06:53,647
Since you caught the thief, Min-gi,

111
00:06:53,713 --> 00:06:57,150
today I'll give you guys
a taste you only get in the country.

112
00:06:57,217 --> 00:07:00,253
I'll treat you to a second delicacy.

113
00:07:00,754 --> 00:07:01,888
A delicacy?

114
00:07:09,496 --> 00:07:10,997
The delicacy is…

115
00:07:11,998 --> 00:07:12,899
grasshoppers?

116
00:07:12,966 --> 00:07:14,601
You said you needed energy?

117
00:07:14,668 --> 00:07:16,369
Grasshoppers are best for that.

118
00:07:17,470 --> 00:07:18,438
Grasshoppers?

119
00:07:18,505 --> 00:07:20,473
You don't know how healthy they are.

120
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,975
Grasshoppers, you see,

121
00:07:22,042 --> 00:07:25,178
treat children's seizures,
whooping cough, and asthma.

122
00:07:25,245 --> 00:07:27,347
They fortify the stomach and spleen,

123
00:07:27,414 --> 00:07:29,316
helping digestion and appetite.

124
00:07:29,382 --> 00:07:31,618
And these hind legs are so developed,

125
00:07:31,685 --> 00:07:33,553
they're mighty powerful.

126
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:36,723
So they're really good for men,

127
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:38,892
but there's no way to describe it.

128
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:41,194
-They're good for men?
-I told you so!

129
00:07:41,261 --> 00:07:42,896
I ate these grasshoppers,

130
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:45,065
and that's how we conceived Min-guk.

131
00:07:50,870 --> 00:07:52,172
Hey, what is this?

132
00:07:52,238 --> 00:07:54,741
It's totally nutty and savory!

133
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:57,210
-Man, this is really good!
-Oh, it's good!

134
00:07:57,277 --> 00:07:58,511
It's so delicious!

135
00:07:59,112 --> 00:08:00,113
Let's catch more!

136
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:03,016
We're all out.
Do you have more grasshoppers, sir?

137
00:08:03,083 --> 00:08:04,985
Grasshoppers? Follow me.

138
00:08:05,051 --> 00:08:06,086
Yes, sir!

139
00:08:15,095 --> 00:08:16,930
Hwa-ran, where are you going?

140
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:19,699
I finished work, so I'm heading home.

141
00:08:19,766 --> 00:08:22,969
-Where are you going?
-To catch grasshoppers.

142
00:08:23,036 --> 00:08:25,672
-Want to come along?
-Yes, I'll come along too.

143
00:08:25,739 --> 00:08:27,674
Hop on.

144
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:32,312
Hold on tight, it's dangerous.

145
00:08:32,979 --> 00:08:34,280
Here we go!

146
00:08:43,656 --> 00:08:45,091
Why am I like this again?

147
00:08:45,158 --> 00:08:47,761
Her arm just grazed mine.
Why's my heart racing?

148
00:08:47,827 --> 00:08:50,330
Have I really fallen for Hwa-ran?

149
00:08:50,397 --> 00:08:52,465
No, there's no way.

150
00:08:52,532 --> 00:08:55,435
Yes, it must be that kind of feeling.

151
00:08:56,069 --> 00:08:57,437
Here's your ramen.

152
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:01,408
Oh, no! What do I do?

153
00:09:01,474 --> 00:09:02,675
I'm so sorry.

154
00:09:02,742 --> 00:09:04,978
Oh, sorry.

155
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:07,280
The snack bar girl
spilled my ramen soup.

156
00:09:07,347 --> 00:09:10,150
Hurriedly wiping up,
she brushed my skin by accident.

157
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:12,318
I guess I was just flustered?

158
00:09:14,154 --> 00:09:16,790
Your heart can race
when you're flustered, right?

159
00:09:16,856 --> 00:09:18,224
A girl's skin grazed mine,

160
00:09:18,291 --> 00:09:20,226
so how could my heart not race?

161
00:09:20,293 --> 00:09:22,429
This could happen to any guy.

162
00:09:22,495 --> 00:09:24,130
It's just a natural reaction.

163
00:09:24,197 --> 00:09:25,932
I'm sure of it.

164
00:09:36,342 --> 00:09:38,311
We're here. Get out.

165
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:44,317
-There's nothing out here.
-They're all over the place!

166
00:09:44,384 --> 00:09:47,754
Catch all you want,
and chew, chomp, taste, and enjoy!

167
00:09:47,821 --> 00:09:49,622
They're free! Get out.

168
00:09:49,689 --> 00:09:51,724
I don't see anything.

169
00:10:01,201 --> 00:10:03,470
-Did you get it?
-I got it.

170
00:10:05,939 --> 00:10:08,208
Oh! I caught one!

171
00:10:16,549 --> 00:10:19,686
Look how nice and plump this one is.

172
00:10:27,894 --> 00:10:29,762
Did you catch a lot?

173
00:10:31,598 --> 00:10:34,000
Come on, is this all you caught?

174
00:10:34,067 --> 00:10:37,137
-Would you like some help?
-I'm fine, so please go away.

175
00:10:39,372 --> 00:10:41,641
That's not how you do it.

176
00:10:41,708 --> 00:10:43,776
Watch closely how I do it.

177
00:11:03,763 --> 00:11:05,832
What? Why is my heart racing again?

178
00:11:05,899 --> 00:11:08,268
Why do this
over her catching grasshoppers?

179
00:11:08,935 --> 00:11:12,071
Did I really fall for her? Is that it?

180
00:11:12,705 --> 00:11:14,807
No, there's no way.

181
00:11:14,874 --> 00:11:18,411
Right, it's that kind of feeling.

182
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:21,414
-Enjoy your meal.
-Thank you.

183
00:11:40,867 --> 00:11:44,137
I thought the snack bar girl
only made good rice cake ramen,

184
00:11:44,204 --> 00:11:47,574
until I learned she also made
great spaghetti and felt…

185
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:50,243
that sense of surprise, I guess?

186
00:11:50,310 --> 00:11:52,979
When you're surprised,
a racing heart is natural…

187
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:56,382
I mean, what's natural about that?
Does that make any sense?

188
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:58,418
Oh, come on, even so,

189
00:11:58,484 --> 00:12:02,355
my heart can't possibly race
watching her catch grasshoppers!

190
00:12:04,624 --> 00:12:06,593
Did you see that?

191
00:12:08,494 --> 00:12:10,129
Ki-jun?

192
00:12:13,199 --> 00:12:14,834
Ki-jun.

193
00:12:15,468 --> 00:12:17,036
Get out of my way!

194
00:12:18,771 --> 00:12:20,907
A girl who catches grasshoppers!

195
00:12:22,442 --> 00:12:24,477
Ki-jun.

196
00:12:27,914 --> 00:12:29,515
I'm home.

197
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:31,584
You're back? Did you have lunch?

198
00:12:31,651 --> 00:12:34,420
I had a snack at Sun-bun's place.

199
00:12:34,487 --> 00:12:35,488
Oh, really?

200
00:12:35,555 --> 00:12:38,358
The guys said they're eating
grasshoppers instead.

201
00:12:39,292 --> 00:12:43,363
-I'd better go grocery shopping.
-What are you shopping for?

202
00:12:43,429 --> 00:12:45,198
Since Min-gi caught the thief,

203
00:12:45,265 --> 00:12:46,966
I'll make him something tasty.

204
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,902
What could I make that he'd like?

205
00:12:49,969 --> 00:12:51,237
Um, Auntie?

206
00:12:51,304 --> 00:12:53,306
I'll do the cooking today.

207
00:13:07,687 --> 00:13:09,122
Hello? Is anyone here?

208
00:13:14,494 --> 00:13:16,629
Ma'am, could I get some carrots?

209
00:13:49,862 --> 00:13:51,731
Yun-hui, do you have a toothpick?

210
00:13:51,798 --> 00:13:53,199
Why a toothpick?

211
00:13:53,266 --> 00:13:55,435
Grasshopper legs are stuck in my teeth.

212
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:57,537
These things really get stuck.

213
00:13:59,339 --> 00:14:01,040
So, what are you making?

214
00:14:03,376 --> 00:14:05,545
-Oh, you're making spaghetti.
-Yes.

215
00:14:06,212 --> 00:14:08,848
Are you making spaghetti for Min-gi

216
00:14:08,915 --> 00:14:10,717
since he said he wanted some?

217
00:14:11,384 --> 00:14:13,686
You secretly look out for Min-gi.

218
00:14:13,753 --> 00:14:15,955
Me? Uh… when did I ever?

219
00:14:16,656 --> 00:14:19,492
I'm just making it
because I want some! Honestly.

220
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,929
Stammering makes you more suspicious.

221
00:14:22,995 --> 00:14:26,165
Yun-hui, let me help. I'm a good cook.

222
00:14:26,232 --> 00:14:27,867
Hey, forget it. I'm fine.

223
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:36,609
Hey! Get out!

224
00:14:36,676 --> 00:14:37,877
I said get out!

225
00:14:37,944 --> 00:14:39,779
Yun-hui, it really was a mistake.

226
00:14:39,846 --> 00:14:42,181
I can really help properly this time.

227
00:14:42,248 --> 00:14:44,384
Should I clean this up? I'm sorry.

228
00:14:44,450 --> 00:14:46,018
You little punk, I swear…

229
00:14:46,085 --> 00:14:48,688
Darn it, I worked so hard
chopping those onions!

230
00:14:48,755 --> 00:14:50,189
You chop all of them now.

231
00:14:50,256 --> 00:14:52,091
Does it actually taste good?

232
00:14:52,158 --> 00:14:54,260
Is it good?

233
00:14:55,595 --> 00:14:57,530
Wow, it's delicious!

234
00:14:57,597 --> 00:15:00,433
-Really?
-Yes, I'll chop the onions for you.

235
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:01,634
Sure, go ahead.

236
00:15:01,701 --> 00:15:04,670
If you chop the onions, what do I do?

237
00:15:07,039 --> 00:15:08,207
Min-gi will love this.

238
00:15:08,274 --> 00:15:11,377
I told you, this isn't for Min-gi.

239
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:24,991
This looks delicious!

240
00:15:25,057 --> 00:15:27,093
Freeze!

241
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:30,129
Eat when the guys get here.
Have some loyalty, you punk…

242
00:15:32,298 --> 00:15:35,968
Why are the boys taking so long?

243
00:15:36,035 --> 00:15:38,004
I'll go out and look for them.

244
00:15:38,070 --> 00:15:39,372
I'll go too, Yun-hui.

245
00:15:39,439 --> 00:15:41,073
No, don't bother.

246
00:15:42,074 --> 00:15:44,844
The food's all ready.
Where on earth did they…

247
00:15:44,911 --> 00:15:46,946
-Close the door tight.
-Okay.

248
00:15:48,247 --> 00:15:50,450
Oh, Min-gi, you're just getting back?

249
00:15:50,516 --> 00:15:51,851
Yes.

250
00:15:52,852 --> 00:15:56,622
-Why are you alone? The others?
-I don't know, they got sidetracked.

251
00:15:56,689 --> 00:15:59,258
I set the food inside. Let's go eat.

252
00:16:03,763 --> 00:16:05,431
Oh, Yu-na!

253
00:16:05,498 --> 00:16:07,033
What made you call?

254
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:10,736
You have a show out here?

255
00:16:11,771 --> 00:16:13,139
What?

256
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:16,142
Sure, okay, got it!

257
00:16:16,209 --> 00:16:17,477
Okay, see you.

258
00:16:18,177 --> 00:16:19,812
Hey, where are you going?

259
00:16:19,879 --> 00:16:22,114
Yu-na's nearby for a show and has time.

260
00:16:22,181 --> 00:16:23,950
She asked me to eat. Back soon!

261
00:16:24,016 --> 00:16:25,551
Um, wait…

262
00:16:30,857 --> 00:16:33,526
Gosh, what's taking them so long?

263
00:16:40,366 --> 00:16:43,202
What? I heard Min-gi.
Why isn't he coming in?

264
00:16:44,437 --> 00:16:46,272
He said he had plans and left.

265
00:16:46,339 --> 00:16:47,373
Really?

266
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:49,242
Then who's going to eat all this?

267
00:16:49,308 --> 00:16:51,444
It'll all be thrown out. What a waste.

268
00:16:51,511 --> 00:16:53,045
Seriously.

269
00:16:53,112 --> 00:16:54,814
Why would we throw it out?

270
00:16:54,881 --> 00:16:57,083
All right, heave-ho!

271
00:16:57,149 --> 00:16:59,952
I'll eat it all, so please don't worry.

272
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:02,722
All of this?
You'll get a stomachache, kid.

273
00:17:02,788 --> 00:17:04,657
I'll be fine.

274
00:17:08,427 --> 00:17:10,062
Mmm, this is delicious!

275
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:14,000
But aren't you going to eat?

276
00:17:14,066 --> 00:17:16,402
I don't really feel like eating.

277
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:19,572
Um, please enjoy the food, everyone.

278
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:28,848
It's good.

279
00:17:32,418 --> 00:17:33,553
Thank goodness.

280
00:17:33,619 --> 00:17:36,188
I guess he really won't show up today.

281
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:42,194
How many days did I waste already
because of that guy? Jeez.

282
00:17:42,261 --> 00:17:45,731
I'll get rid of him soon,
no matter what it takes.

283
00:17:49,368 --> 00:17:50,903
Su-yeon!

284
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:55,241
Where to at this hour?

285
00:17:56,676 --> 00:18:00,746
Just out for a walk.
What brings you out so late again?

286
00:18:00,813 --> 00:18:03,950
When a boyfriend visits his girlfriend,

287
00:18:04,016 --> 00:18:07,553
-does day or night really matter?
-Sure.

288
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:09,956
Plus, I have something to give you.

289
00:18:10,623 --> 00:18:12,158
What is it?

290
00:18:14,493 --> 00:18:17,263
-Ta-da!
-What is this?

291
00:18:21,701 --> 00:18:23,803
Easy, don't panic. Please don't panic.

292
00:18:23,869 --> 00:18:25,771
It's just grasshoppers, that's all.

293
00:18:25,838 --> 00:18:28,808
They may look a bit gross,
but they taste amazing.

294
00:18:28,874 --> 00:18:31,744
-Here, try one.
-No, thanks. I'm not eating that.

295
00:18:31,811 --> 00:18:34,113
Come on, don't be like that. Try one.

296
00:18:34,180 --> 00:18:35,448
I said no, thanks!

297
00:18:36,082 --> 00:18:37,984
Do it for the effort I put in.

298
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:40,519
-Just eat one…
-I told you, no!

299
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:54,400
Uh, Su-yeon, this…

300
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:55,868
-Ow!
-What did you touch?

301
00:18:55,935 --> 00:18:58,437
No, that's not what I meant. I just…

302
00:18:58,504 --> 00:18:59,538
You crazy bastard!

303
00:18:59,605 --> 00:19:01,207
If I say I won't eat, I won't!

304
00:19:01,273 --> 00:19:02,875
Why the fuck don't you get it?

305
00:19:02,942 --> 00:19:05,077
I'll rip your damn ears right off!

306
00:19:06,545 --> 00:19:08,381
You'd say that to your boyfriend?

307
00:19:08,447 --> 00:19:11,584
Boyfriend? Quit spouting horseshit!

308
00:19:11,651 --> 00:19:14,453
Don't ever get in my damn sight again.

309
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:17,356
Bother me one more time,
and your damn skull, bam!

310
00:19:17,423 --> 00:19:19,825
I'll smash it to pieces, got that?

311
00:19:34,473 --> 00:19:37,243
To think I… a grasshopper…

312
00:19:38,711 --> 00:19:41,347
I fell for a woman
catching grasshoppers…

313
00:19:41,414 --> 00:19:43,049
Wow!

314
00:19:43,983 --> 00:19:45,785
Grasshoppers of all things, jeez.

315
00:19:52,792 --> 00:19:53,993
Han-cheol.

316
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:56,362
Are you crying? What's wrong?

317
00:19:57,163 --> 00:19:58,731
Ki-jun…

318
00:19:59,298 --> 00:20:00,833
I got dumped by Su-yeon.

319
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:04,437
You said you started dating yesterday!
Why? Because of what?

320
00:20:07,373 --> 00:20:08,908
Because of grasshoppers.

321
00:20:11,644 --> 00:20:13,079
Grasshoppers?

322
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,449
Grasshoppers are ruining people today.

323
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,122
These actually taste really good…

324
00:20:30,563 --> 00:20:31,931
He should be here by now.

325
00:20:38,204 --> 00:20:40,840
-Hello?
-Hey, where are you right now?

326
00:20:42,308 --> 00:20:44,410
I said to come back right after work!

327
00:20:44,477 --> 00:20:46,011
I said I won't go to those.

328
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:49,882
If you keep this up,
I can't promise your next album.

329
00:20:49,949 --> 00:20:53,119
If you don't come right now,
you're done. Done!

330
00:21:18,177 --> 00:21:19,378
YU-NA

331
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:24,116
-I'm almost there--
-Min-gi.

332
00:21:24,183 --> 00:21:27,920
Sorry, something urgent came up,
so I think I have to head back.

333
00:21:28,621 --> 00:21:32,091
It can't be helped, then.

334
00:21:32,158 --> 00:21:35,294
I was just about to head out anyway.

335
00:21:36,061 --> 00:21:37,930
-I'm really sorry.
-It's okay.

336
00:21:37,997 --> 00:21:40,166
Really, don't worry about me.

337
00:21:40,232 --> 00:21:41,901
Have a safe trip back.

338
00:21:59,285 --> 00:22:01,420
At least I got to see her face.

339
00:22:20,372 --> 00:22:23,342
I'll do it. Go away.

340
00:22:24,243 --> 00:22:26,278
I have nothing to do, so I'll help.

341
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:28,948
I already told you it's fine.

342
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:37,489
Yun-hui, what's with that look
you've had since earlier?

343
00:22:38,991 --> 00:22:42,528
Is it because of Min-gi?

344
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:48,267
No! Why would it be about Min-gi?

345
00:22:48,334 --> 00:22:50,169
I'm completely fine.

346
00:22:50,936 --> 00:22:54,039
Besides, whatever look I have,
what does it matter to you?

347
00:22:54,707 --> 00:22:56,742
-It does matter to me.
-Why would it?

348
00:22:56,809 --> 00:22:57,943
Because I care.

349
00:22:58,010 --> 00:23:02,648
Why on earth do you care, then? Why?

350
00:23:02,715 --> 00:23:04,717
Because I like you.

351
00:23:05,885 --> 00:23:07,186
What?

352
00:23:07,253 --> 00:23:08,854
I said I like you.

353
00:23:15,694 --> 00:23:18,697
You think I'll fall for that again?

354
00:23:18,764 --> 00:23:21,834
Everything's a joke to you, you punk.
Every single thing!

355
00:23:21,901 --> 00:23:24,103
Gosh, seriously…

356
00:23:25,037 --> 00:23:27,072
It's not a joke.

357
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:42,388
Yun-hui.

358
00:23:43,022 --> 00:23:46,525
Do my eyes look like they're lying?

359
00:23:48,494 --> 00:23:50,596
Look closely.

360
00:23:52,765 --> 00:23:54,533
Even if lips can lie,

361
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:58,504
the eyes can't lie.

362
00:24:00,739 --> 00:24:02,308
Don't you know that saying?

363
00:24:10,516 --> 00:24:11,550
Oh, gosh!

364
00:24:11,617 --> 00:24:14,486
You take me for a fool, a total fool!

365
00:24:14,553 --> 00:24:17,356
Hey, I fell for it once.
Would I fall for it twice?

366
00:24:17,423 --> 00:24:19,925
I could smack you! Go to bed already!

367
00:24:19,992 --> 00:24:21,894
It's all because of those pests…

368
00:24:21,961 --> 00:24:23,395
I can't take it, I can't!

369
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:24,897
Honestly…

370
00:24:30,035 --> 00:24:31,704
I really mean it…

371
00:24:59,598 --> 00:25:02,434
You crazy bastard!
If I say I won't eat, I won't!

372
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:04,303
Why can't you take a damn hint?

373
00:25:04,370 --> 00:25:05,871
I'll yank your ears off!

374
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:30,396
Why are you kids sighing this morning

375
00:25:30,462 --> 00:25:32,531
and harmonizing like a choir?

376
00:25:34,333 --> 00:25:37,302
Ow, my stomach, my stomach.

377
00:25:37,369 --> 00:25:40,372
What a stench! Right before breakfast,

378
00:25:40,439 --> 00:25:43,075
why do you keep running to the toilet?

379
00:25:43,142 --> 00:25:44,410
I don't know.

380
00:25:44,476 --> 00:25:47,946
I didn't get a wink of sleep
running to the bathroom all night.

381
00:25:48,013 --> 00:25:51,817
No wonder your stomach hurts
after eating all that spaghetti.

382
00:25:52,851 --> 00:25:56,055
Spaghetti? You had spaghetti yesterday?

383
00:25:56,121 --> 00:26:00,359
Yes, Yun-hui made it. It was so good…

384
00:26:03,562 --> 00:26:05,731
You had spaghetti by yourselves again?

385
00:26:05,798 --> 00:26:08,200
Why? You met Yu-na or Yuzu or whoever

386
00:26:08,267 --> 00:26:10,702
and ate something way better, right?

387
00:26:13,205 --> 00:26:14,506
I didn't even see her.

388
00:26:14,573 --> 00:26:17,342
Oh, you got stood up!

389
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:19,378
Serves you right, you jerk!

390
00:26:20,312 --> 00:26:22,448
Why are you picking a fight so early?

391
00:26:22,514 --> 00:26:24,083
When did I? When did I?

392
00:26:24,149 --> 00:26:26,985
Forget it.
I want spaghetti too. Make me some.

393
00:26:27,052 --> 00:26:30,489
No way!
If you want some, make it yourself.

394
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:34,293
Hey, where are you going
in the middle of eating?

395
00:26:35,227 --> 00:26:38,163
That old lady is really
snapping at me this morning.

396
00:26:38,230 --> 00:26:41,200
How do you two fight whenever you meet?

397
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:43,035
You'll fall for each other.

398
00:26:43,869 --> 00:26:47,072
Fall for each other?
How can you say something so hideous?

399
00:26:53,045 --> 00:26:56,548
It hurts, it hurts, it hurts.

400
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:58,383
My arm hurts.

401
00:27:00,052 --> 00:27:01,653
Ow, my arm.

402
00:27:02,321 --> 00:27:04,957
Did I drink too much rice wine
with one hand?

403
00:27:05,023 --> 00:27:07,226
Why is my left arm so numb?

404
00:27:08,894 --> 00:27:10,529
What is this?

405
00:27:14,266 --> 00:27:15,968
Mi-young?

406
00:27:16,034 --> 00:27:17,703
Why is she here?

407
00:27:21,039 --> 00:27:22,774
Are you awake, honey?

408
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:26,178
Honey?

409
00:27:26,245 --> 00:27:29,381
"Honey"? What are you talking about?

410
00:27:29,448 --> 00:27:32,651
What else would I call my husband?

411
00:27:33,652 --> 00:27:38,357
Honey, I'm so tired.
I'll sleep a little longer.

412
00:27:47,866 --> 00:27:52,070
Since that didn't hurt,
it's a dream. Just a dream.

413
00:27:53,138 --> 00:27:55,841
Ever since Hyori married Sang-soon,

414
00:27:55,908 --> 00:27:59,711
she stopped showing up,
and now it's starting again. Again.

415
00:28:01,013 --> 00:28:04,983
But why did Mi-young show up?

416
00:28:05,751 --> 00:28:07,686
That's so weird.

417
00:28:23,402 --> 00:28:25,103
Ow, what is this?

418
00:28:28,207 --> 00:28:29,341
Grandpa.

419
00:28:29,408 --> 00:28:31,710
You're awake? I'm sorry.

420
00:28:31,777 --> 00:28:34,780
I came in looking for something, and…

421
00:28:34,846 --> 00:28:36,515
Want to put it in here?

422
00:28:45,857 --> 00:28:48,560
I'll leave this here. Want some?

423
00:28:48,627 --> 00:28:51,997
I don't want any. I really don't.

424
00:28:52,598 --> 00:28:54,866
By the way, where is Mom?

425
00:28:54,933 --> 00:28:57,035
She went to a prayer retreat

426
00:28:57,102 --> 00:28:59,104
to pray you get married off.

427
00:28:59,171 --> 00:29:02,174
She said she's doing
a 100-day fasting prayer.

428
00:29:05,244 --> 00:29:08,513
Gosh, Mom is really too much…

429
00:29:09,448 --> 00:29:13,318
Anyway, why did I dream of Mi-young?

430
00:29:13,919 --> 00:29:15,554
That's strange.

431
00:29:27,499 --> 00:29:29,368
She still hasn't sent the money.

432
00:29:29,434 --> 00:29:32,838
Is she testing my patience? Damn it.

433
00:29:40,946 --> 00:29:43,682
I'm dead tired.
Why bug me with a call this early?

434
00:29:43,749 --> 00:29:46,718
-Why haven't you sent my pay?
-Your pay?

435
00:29:47,686 --> 00:29:51,123
Sorry, sorry. It slipped my mind.

436
00:29:51,189 --> 00:29:55,327
Oh, right. Some guys came by
looking for you at the bar.

437
00:29:55,394 --> 00:29:57,596
For me? Who?

438
00:29:57,663 --> 00:30:01,099
I don't know.
They kept prying into where you were.

439
00:30:01,166 --> 00:30:03,435
They gave me such a rough time.

440
00:30:03,502 --> 00:30:05,437
So did you tell them where I am?

441
00:30:05,504 --> 00:30:08,407
How can I tell them
when I don't know where you are?

442
00:30:08,473 --> 00:30:10,642
Anyway, swear you have no idea.

443
00:30:10,709 --> 00:30:13,145
And never give them my number, got it?

444
00:30:13,211 --> 00:30:17,482
Don't worry.
You know loyalty is my middle name.

445
00:30:17,549 --> 00:30:18,817
Loyalty? Cut the crap.

446
00:30:18,884 --> 00:30:21,253
If you're loyal, just send my money.

447
00:30:24,723 --> 00:30:26,692
Who on earth could it be?

448
00:30:27,759 --> 00:30:31,463
That guy couldn't be awake already.

449
00:30:37,836 --> 00:30:41,540
Director Kang, when do you think
this fellow will wake up?

450
00:30:41,606 --> 00:30:43,141
Well, it's hard to say.

451
00:30:43,208 --> 00:30:46,845
He is in a coma, so I cannot
give you a definite answer right now.

452
00:30:53,919 --> 00:30:55,454
That bastard of an aide.

453
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:57,656
How dare he steal my money?

454
00:30:57,723 --> 00:31:00,425
You punk, I told you to bring him in.

455
00:31:00,492 --> 00:31:01,893
Why'd you nearly kill him?

456
00:31:01,960 --> 00:31:04,563
He bolted into the street.
We couldn't stop it.

457
00:31:04,629 --> 00:31:07,099
Enough talk. Find my money.

458
00:31:07,165 --> 00:31:08,734
Find it, whatever it takes.

459
00:31:08,800 --> 00:31:10,635
Prosecutors suspect a slush fund.

460
00:31:10,702 --> 00:31:13,972
It's fine. I'll handle them myself.

461
00:31:14,039 --> 00:31:16,007
Check that punk's extended family.

462
00:31:16,074 --> 00:31:19,010
Dig through his call logs
and everything to find it.

463
00:31:19,077 --> 00:31:20,112
I already checked.

464
00:31:20,178 --> 00:31:22,581
He often called
a woman at a talking bar.

465
00:31:22,647 --> 00:31:24,149
A talking bar?

466
00:31:25,016 --> 00:31:26,885
She goes by Scarlett at the bar.

467
00:31:26,952 --> 00:31:28,587
They say he was her regular.

468
00:31:28,653 --> 00:31:31,022
I went to the bar,
but she had suddenly quit

469
00:31:31,089 --> 00:31:32,457
and vacated her studio.

470
00:31:32,524 --> 00:31:33,825
It smells a little--

471
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:36,228
-It's fishy.
-So? You'll just sniff around?

472
00:31:36,294 --> 00:31:38,930
Find her no matter what, you punk!

473
00:31:38,997 --> 00:31:41,500
If you don't, you're all dead. Got it?

474
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:42,934
-Yes, sir.
-Understood.

475
00:32:12,731 --> 00:32:14,099
This tastes…

476
00:32:14,166 --> 00:32:17,903
just like the kimchi my mom
used to bury in the ground.

477
00:32:18,603 --> 00:32:21,973
-The food sovereignty of 70 million…
-Here we go, easy does it!

478
00:32:22,040 --> 00:32:23,341
All right, let's eat.

479
00:32:23,408 --> 00:32:24,743
Honey, can I help you?

480
00:32:24,810 --> 00:32:25,877
Nope, nope. No, no.

481
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:29,347
Honey, you just enjoy the food.

482
00:32:29,414 --> 00:32:32,784
Stop it, I've got goosebumps!
I'm turning into a goose here!

483
00:32:32,851 --> 00:32:34,920
If you can't stand it, go get married!

484
00:32:34,986 --> 00:32:37,088
Wipe the sleep from your eyes, brat!

485
00:32:37,155 --> 00:32:39,257
Min-guk's grandma, please eat.

486
00:32:39,324 --> 00:32:42,494
Opening the market unconditionally
after a grace period

487
00:32:42,561 --> 00:32:45,297
is driving farmers
to their deaths, they say.

488
00:32:45,363 --> 00:32:46,731
RICE MARKET PROTESTS GROW

489
00:32:46,798 --> 00:32:48,433
Good grief.

490
00:32:48,500 --> 00:32:52,037
How do they expect farmers to farm?

491
00:32:52,103 --> 00:32:53,205
In other news.

492
00:32:53,271 --> 00:32:55,474
Recently, targeting rural women,

493
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:58,443
illegal cosmetic procedures
have become a major issue.

494
00:32:58,510 --> 00:33:01,713
Those women are out of their minds.

495
00:33:01,780 --> 00:33:03,248
Just what are they doing?

496
00:33:03,315 --> 00:33:05,584
Those women must be crazy!

497
00:33:05,650 --> 00:33:09,287
Oh, their homes must be doing great.

498
00:33:09,354 --> 00:33:11,790
What crazy women. Mom, look at that.

499
00:33:12,958 --> 00:33:15,460
-Why the sunglasses?
-It's nothing.

500
00:33:15,527 --> 00:33:17,496
How is that nothing? Take them off.

501
00:33:17,562 --> 00:33:19,731
Oh, my gosh!

502
00:33:19,798 --> 00:33:23,702
Be sure to consult an expert
and avoid illegal procedures.

503
00:33:24,836 --> 00:33:26,404
What's with your eyebrows?

504
00:33:26,471 --> 00:33:29,040
Wait, on that news report…

505
00:33:29,541 --> 00:33:32,978
was one of those pathetic women
you, Mom?

506
00:33:33,044 --> 00:33:35,680
Um, she said she was an expert

507
00:33:35,747 --> 00:33:38,450
and had a license, so I let her do it.

508
00:33:38,517 --> 00:33:40,986
Man-gu, what do I do about this?

509
00:33:41,052 --> 00:33:43,588
I don't know, Mom. You deal with it.

510
00:33:43,655 --> 00:33:46,458
Man-gu, they say this
can be removed with a laser.

511
00:33:46,525 --> 00:33:48,593
I told you I don't know! You deal…

512
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:50,295
Man-gu…

513
00:33:53,665 --> 00:33:55,300
Gosh, honestly.

514
00:33:55,367 --> 00:33:57,168
Why is she taking so long?

515
00:33:57,235 --> 00:33:59,304
Why call us here so early? Why?

516
00:33:59,371 --> 00:34:02,908
I went to the Soul-myeon
Village Head meeting this morning.

517
00:34:02,974 --> 00:34:06,244
You know it's total chaos
over the rice market opening, right?

518
00:34:06,311 --> 00:34:07,579
-Right.
-Yes.

519
00:34:07,646 --> 00:34:09,714
So our Indi County farmers,

520
00:34:09,781 --> 00:34:11,383
for rice market measures,

521
00:34:11,449 --> 00:34:13,585
will do a three-step relay, they say.

522
00:34:13,652 --> 00:34:14,886
Three steps, one bow?

523
00:34:14,953 --> 00:34:17,455
Yes, two delegates from each village

524
00:34:17,522 --> 00:34:19,891
do 5 km of three steps, one bow
to county hall

525
00:34:19,958 --> 00:34:22,394
and protest directly
to the County Governor.

526
00:34:22,460 --> 00:34:24,863
And Headquarters
Against Rice Market Opening

527
00:34:24,930 --> 00:34:27,499
says they'll broadcast it live online.

528
00:34:27,566 --> 00:34:29,467
How's that? Sounds good, right?

529
00:34:29,534 --> 00:34:31,169
That's a great idea.

530
00:34:31,236 --> 00:34:32,304
But why call us?

531
00:34:32,370 --> 00:34:35,073
I was hoping you two
would represent our village

532
00:34:35,140 --> 00:34:38,176
and do the three steps, one bow.

533
00:34:38,243 --> 00:34:42,047
I heard three steps, one bow
is way harder than you'd think.

534
00:34:42,113 --> 00:34:44,649
So I picked the very youngest men

535
00:34:44,716 --> 00:34:47,485
in our village. No complaints, right?

536
00:34:47,552 --> 00:34:49,220
I have a complaint!

537
00:34:49,287 --> 00:34:50,589
Those punks are younger!

538
00:34:50,655 --> 00:34:54,526
How can I trust them with this?
Who knows what they'll mess up next?

539
00:34:54,593 --> 00:34:56,194
We don't want to, you know.

540
00:34:56,261 --> 00:34:59,097
I wasn't going to ask, you know. Jeez.

541
00:34:59,164 --> 00:35:01,800
Please, you two, please help me out.

542
00:35:01,866 --> 00:35:03,568
Besides, if you don't finish,

543
00:35:03,635 --> 00:35:05,804
it'll disgrace our village nationwide.

544
00:35:05,870 --> 00:35:09,474
Start getting in shape now, got it?

545
00:35:09,541 --> 00:35:11,409
-Okay.
-Got it.

546
00:35:12,077 --> 00:35:14,479
Um, sir, when do we go
to our cabbage field?

547
00:35:14,546 --> 00:35:16,915
Don't rush me, you punks!

548
00:35:16,982 --> 00:35:19,517
Rushing me without even paying tuition…

549
00:35:19,584 --> 00:35:20,719
Tell me about it.

550
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:24,856
What's his problem, seriously?

551
00:35:27,258 --> 00:35:29,694
I got whacked on the head again.

552
00:35:29,761 --> 00:35:32,263
I think all my brain cells died, jeez.

553
00:35:32,330 --> 00:35:35,667
Huh? Hey, who are those guys?

554
00:35:35,734 --> 00:35:37,702
How'd these damn weeds grow so much?

555
00:35:37,769 --> 00:35:40,171
Right? I swear I didn't
see them yesterday.

556
00:35:40,238 --> 00:35:43,608
The inevitable is here,
it's finally here!

557
00:35:43,675 --> 00:35:45,577
Sir, what should we do about this?

558
00:35:45,644 --> 00:35:47,412
What do you think you should do?

559
00:35:47,479 --> 00:35:49,881
You didn't listen,
so pull every single one.

560
00:35:49,948 --> 00:35:51,750
All of them? Can't we leave them?

561
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,718
Sure, leave them. It's fine, fine.

562
00:35:53,785 --> 00:35:57,756
Then these weeds will slurp up
every last nutrient in the soil

563
00:35:57,822 --> 00:36:01,660
and grow into tightly packed weeds,
much sturdier than the cabbages.

564
00:36:01,726 --> 00:36:04,696
Then you can pull and sell
weeds instead of cabbages.

565
00:36:05,563 --> 00:36:07,599
I'm losing my mind.

566
00:36:07,666 --> 00:36:10,502
The water deer left.
Now come tightly packed weeds.

567
00:36:10,568 --> 00:36:12,203
See? What did I tell you?

568
00:36:12,270 --> 00:36:13,672
Didn't I say use plastic?

569
00:36:13,738 --> 00:36:15,974
We don't have money for plastic.

570
00:36:16,041 --> 00:36:18,777
And we can just pull
these measly weeds like this.

571
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:20,512
You punks have no fear.

572
00:36:20,578 --> 00:36:23,014
You don't know
what scary monsters weeds are.

573
00:36:23,081 --> 00:36:24,883
Pfft, scary? Please.

574
00:36:24,949 --> 00:36:27,352
You just pull puny weeds like this.

575
00:36:27,419 --> 00:36:29,220
I'll pull some. Watch closely.

576
00:36:29,287 --> 00:36:30,722
Just rip them like this?

577
00:36:30,789 --> 00:36:33,358
-See? Hey, let's start.
-They come right out.

578
00:36:33,425 --> 00:36:35,960
Sir, why don't weeds grow
under the plastic?

579
00:36:36,027 --> 00:36:38,496
They can't get sunlight under plastic.

580
00:36:38,563 --> 00:36:40,331
-Pull the weeds.
-Hup!

581
00:36:40,932 --> 00:36:42,734
See? I pulled it right out.

582
00:36:42,801 --> 00:36:44,536
Sure, pull them. Pull them out.

583
00:36:46,971 --> 00:36:49,340
That's simple. Nothing to it. Hmph.

584
00:36:49,407 --> 00:36:51,209
Sure, sure. Go ahead, go ahead.

585
00:36:51,276 --> 00:36:53,244
Go ahead!

586
00:36:53,812 --> 00:36:54,679
THE NEXT DAY

587
00:36:54,746 --> 00:36:57,982
What? I definitely
pulled them all yesterday.

588
00:36:59,384 --> 00:37:00,518
No way.

589
00:37:00,585 --> 00:37:03,655
They grew this much overnight?

590
00:37:04,289 --> 00:37:06,458
Shouldn't we have pulled the roots too?

591
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:10,628
Okay, then today
we pull them out by the roots.

592
00:37:10,695 --> 00:37:12,931
Take a furrow each. One, two, three!

593
00:37:12,997 --> 00:37:14,632
Let's do this!

594
00:37:20,505 --> 00:37:24,275
Die, die, you weeds, die!

595
00:37:29,114 --> 00:37:32,517
THE DAY AFTER THAT

596
00:37:37,255 --> 00:37:40,458
AND THE DAY AFTER THAT

597
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:47,599
What on earth are these guys?

598
00:37:48,633 --> 00:37:51,336
We definitely pulled
every last root yesterday.

599
00:37:51,870 --> 00:37:53,638
How does this make any sense?

600
00:37:53,705 --> 00:37:56,141
My, my, the weeds sure grew a lot.

601
00:37:56,207 --> 00:37:58,243
See? What did I tell you?

602
00:37:58,309 --> 00:38:02,647
Those things are zombies, zombies.
They always come back no matter what.

603
00:38:02,714 --> 00:38:04,215
They're phoenixes.

604
00:38:04,282 --> 00:38:06,651
This is seriously driving me crazy.

605
00:38:07,519 --> 00:38:09,554
What are you doing here right now?

606
00:38:09,621 --> 00:38:12,323
I have to do Three steps, one bow
in a few days.

607
00:38:12,390 --> 00:38:15,260
So I'm building up my stamina. Why?

608
00:38:21,966 --> 00:38:25,270
Wow, you're trendier than you look.

609
00:38:25,336 --> 00:38:28,807
Looks aside, I'm an early adopter.
An early adopter.

610
00:38:28,873 --> 00:38:32,777
I'm the first to order new farm tools
straight from overseas, that's me.

611
00:38:32,844 --> 00:38:34,212
Oh, even from overseas.

612
00:38:34,279 --> 00:38:37,549
Anyway, unless you want to grow old
and die pulling weeds,

613
00:38:37,615 --> 00:38:40,118
just put plastic on it
while I'm asking nicely.

614
00:38:40,185 --> 00:38:41,820
How much is the plastic?

615
00:38:41,886 --> 00:38:44,656
At the Return-to-Farm
Comprehensive Support Center,

616
00:38:44,722 --> 00:38:46,891
should I ask
a Return-to-Farm Consultant?

617
00:38:46,958 --> 00:38:49,427
Return-to-Farm
Comprehensive Support Center?

618
00:38:49,494 --> 00:38:51,563
Yes, for people moving to the country,

619
00:38:51,629 --> 00:38:54,332
it teaches farming
and helps them settle in.

620
00:38:54,399 --> 00:38:57,335
Actually, I'm Hadong-ri's
Return-to-Farm Doctor.

621
00:38:57,402 --> 00:38:59,337
A doctor.

622
00:39:00,004 --> 00:39:01,739
Oh, a call came right on time.

623
00:39:01,806 --> 00:39:04,642
-So trendy, so trendy.
-Oh!

624
00:39:04,709 --> 00:39:05,977
RETURN-TO-FARM CENTER

625
00:39:06,644 --> 00:39:08,746
Hey, what brings you to call?

626
00:39:08,813 --> 00:39:10,048
Oh, that?

627
00:39:10,114 --> 00:39:12,584
Okay, I'll try to carve out some time.

628
00:39:12,650 --> 00:39:15,620
Oh, and here in our village,

629
00:39:15,687 --> 00:39:17,689
some guys came here to farm, you see.

630
00:39:17,755 --> 00:39:21,459
They need to put plastic mulch
on their cabbage field, and it's hard.

631
00:39:21,526 --> 00:39:23,928
Is there any way to help them out?

632
00:39:23,995 --> 00:39:25,997
Okay, look into it and call me back.

633
00:39:26,064 --> 00:39:28,399
Okay, thanks. Got it.

634
00:39:28,466 --> 00:39:30,101
Right, right. End.

635
00:39:31,936 --> 00:39:34,205
Just wait, they'll call back.

636
00:39:34,272 --> 00:39:37,342
Um… I'm just asking in case,

637
00:39:37,408 --> 00:39:39,911
but how much is it if we just buy it?

638
00:39:39,978 --> 00:39:41,746
With a 10,000-pyeong field,

639
00:39:41,813 --> 00:39:45,149
plus pins to hold the plastic
and all, about five million won?

640
00:39:46,317 --> 00:39:47,585
Five million?

641
00:39:48,119 --> 00:39:49,821
Han-cheol, how much do we have?

642
00:39:49,888 --> 00:39:53,324
About a million won.
Hey, not even close. Not even close.

643
00:39:55,860 --> 00:39:57,295
Um, listen here.

644
00:39:57,362 --> 00:40:00,231
Then how about we do it like this?

645
00:40:09,807 --> 00:40:11,342
Two million.

646
00:40:11,976 --> 00:40:15,480
Come on, you said driving
a foreign car once in your life

647
00:40:15,546 --> 00:40:16,981
was your lifelong wish.

648
00:40:17,815 --> 00:40:19,117
Four million.

649
00:40:19,183 --> 00:40:21,719
-2.5 million.
-Come on, seriously.

650
00:40:21,786 --> 00:40:24,422
This is a convertible, a convertible.

651
00:40:24,489 --> 00:40:27,025
The top opens up like this.

652
00:40:27,091 --> 00:40:29,060
3.5 million won.

653
00:40:29,127 --> 00:40:32,196
Three million, no higher.
Take it or leave it.

654
00:40:32,263 --> 00:40:34,232
All right, all right.

655
00:40:34,832 --> 00:40:36,868
He really drives a hard bargain.

656
00:40:36,935 --> 00:40:39,904
I'll bring you crisp cash later.

657
00:40:39,971 --> 00:40:41,339
Car keys.

658
00:40:44,042 --> 00:40:45,476
Yes!

659
00:40:45,543 --> 00:40:47,345
Sir, please take good care of it.

660
00:40:47,412 --> 00:40:49,113
I've had this car for so long.

661
00:40:49,180 --> 00:40:50,315
Sir!

662
00:40:50,381 --> 00:40:53,151
-You can't step on it like that!
-Yes!

663
00:40:53,217 --> 00:40:54,752
Sir…

664
00:40:54,819 --> 00:40:57,588
I'll definitely get this back someday.

665
00:40:57,655 --> 00:40:58,856
Take good care of it.

666
00:40:58,923 --> 00:41:01,292
KITT, let's go! Come on!

667
00:41:05,196 --> 00:41:06,564
We even sold off the car.

668
00:41:06,631 --> 00:41:09,100
How did we end up like this? Darn it.

669
00:41:10,234 --> 00:41:13,638
-Are you okay?
-Ha, I'm fine, I'm fine.

670
00:41:13,705 --> 00:41:15,239
Hey, we made 500,000 won!

671
00:41:15,306 --> 00:41:17,976
I bought it at a junkyard
for 2.5 million won.

672
00:41:18,042 --> 00:41:19,577
Oh, yes!

673
00:41:20,211 --> 00:41:23,147
You con-artist bastard.
Still, good job, good job.

674
00:41:23,214 --> 00:41:27,085
What good does that do?
We're still a million won short.

675
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:28,553
That's true.

676
00:41:28,619 --> 00:41:31,656
Is there really nowhere to get money?

677
00:41:36,260 --> 00:41:38,363
There is, there is!

678
00:41:39,964 --> 00:41:42,266
What are you thinking? Playing Hwatu?

679
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:47,105
I may not be good at studying,
but I'm a wizard at games like this.

680
00:41:47,171 --> 00:41:50,341
Coin games, page-flipping,
Go-Stop, poker, and so on.

681
00:41:50,408 --> 00:41:51,743
I was good at them all.

682
00:41:51,809 --> 00:41:53,911
Whenever I show up, the game

683
00:41:53,978 --> 00:41:55,246
is always over.

684
00:41:55,313 --> 00:41:59,317
You won't win much off country elders…

685
00:41:59,384 --> 00:42:01,886
Hey, every little bit helps.

686
00:42:01,953 --> 00:42:05,323
Why just sit around?
We're desperate for every penny.

687
00:42:05,390 --> 00:42:07,325
Trust me and follow my lead.

688
00:42:09,594 --> 00:42:12,930
I see you're playing Go-Stop.

689
00:42:12,997 --> 00:42:16,300
Yes, just to pass the time.

690
00:42:16,367 --> 00:42:18,269
We're playing for ten won a point.

691
00:42:20,905 --> 00:42:23,207
I'm bored too. May I join you?

692
00:42:23,274 --> 00:42:25,076
Sure, if you want.

693
00:42:38,790 --> 00:42:40,858
What's wrong with that guy?

694
00:42:46,030 --> 00:42:50,835
Um, sir, ten won a point
doesn't have much thrill to it.

695
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:53,438
-How about 100 won a point?
-100 won a point?

696
00:42:54,205 --> 00:42:55,773
Sure, why not.

697
00:42:59,811 --> 00:43:01,479
Then shall I shuffle?

698
00:43:01,546 --> 00:43:03,381
-Go ahead.
-Yes, yes.

699
00:43:11,756 --> 00:43:13,424
All right, shall we begin?

700
00:43:13,491 --> 00:43:15,793
-Sure.
-Then I'll go first.

701
00:43:15,860 --> 00:43:17,261
All right.

702
00:43:23,634 --> 00:43:25,036
Oh, no.

703
00:43:28,406 --> 00:43:31,609
Gosh, that's a Godori bird alert.

704
00:43:32,176 --> 00:43:34,145
Come on, Grandpa.

705
00:43:34,212 --> 00:43:35,646
After just one move,

706
00:43:35,713 --> 00:43:38,449
are you really building up
the tension already?

707
00:43:38,516 --> 00:43:42,320
I'm fine. I won't go down easily.

708
00:43:42,386 --> 00:43:44,088
I need to capture this one.

709
00:43:44,155 --> 00:43:46,357
Take the paulownia card, then this…

710
00:43:48,493 --> 00:43:51,462
My, how can I thank you for this?

711
00:43:52,029 --> 00:43:55,633
-Now, hand over a Pi card.
-Okay.

712
00:44:00,538 --> 00:44:02,673
You sure are lucky.

713
00:44:02,740 --> 00:44:04,275
Here I go.

714
00:44:04,876 --> 00:44:08,513
Wow, there are no Pi cards to take.

715
00:44:10,448 --> 00:44:12,984
Oh, look, that's Godori.

716
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:19,290
Three Gwang and Godori is eight points.

717
00:44:19,357 --> 00:44:21,459
-I can score already.
-Already?

718
00:44:21,526 --> 00:44:23,694
Plus a Hongdan ribbon alert.

719
00:44:26,097 --> 00:44:27,932
One-Go.

720
00:44:28,566 --> 00:44:30,201
One-Go?

721
00:44:33,371 --> 00:44:34,972
All right.

722
00:44:43,748 --> 00:44:45,049
What is this?

723
00:44:46,017 --> 00:44:47,251
Hongdan.

724
00:44:48,352 --> 00:44:51,255
-Two-Go.
-Two-Go?

725
00:44:52,757 --> 00:44:54,492
Darn it, I don't care.

726
00:44:59,163 --> 00:45:00,331
Cheongdan.

727
00:45:03,134 --> 00:45:04,835
Three-Go.

728
00:45:11,375 --> 00:45:13,211
Don't touch my Ppeok stack!

729
00:45:13,277 --> 00:45:15,713
Give me a Pi card.

730
00:45:16,581 --> 00:45:17,982
Yes, sir.

731
00:45:21,619 --> 00:45:23,020
Four-Go.

732
00:45:26,357 --> 00:45:28,626
-Five-Go.
-Five…

733
00:45:31,095 --> 00:45:32,997
Six-Go.

734
00:45:34,999 --> 00:45:37,235
-Seven-Go.
-Seven?

735
00:45:40,938 --> 00:45:42,607
Eight-Go!

736
00:45:51,515 --> 00:45:55,453
-Sir, how many points is that?
-Gosh, it's hard to even count.

737
00:45:55,519 --> 00:45:58,623
First, it's eight points for Eight-Go.

738
00:45:58,689 --> 00:46:02,159
Plus Five Gwang, Cheongdan,
Hongdan, Chodan,

739
00:46:02,226 --> 00:46:03,794
and Godori.

740
00:46:03,861 --> 00:46:07,765
Add the Pi, ten-point cards, and Ddi,

741
00:46:08,833 --> 00:46:10,101
and that's 55 points.

742
00:46:10,167 --> 00:46:14,071
With the Pibak, Gwangbak,
and Meongtta penalties,

743
00:46:14,138 --> 00:46:16,173
plus the Eight-Go multiplier,

744
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:17,675
that's 1,024 times.

745
00:46:17,742 --> 00:46:21,579
The total is 64,512 points.

746
00:46:21,646 --> 00:46:23,914
It's 100 won a point.

747
00:46:23,981 --> 00:46:27,818
So you owe 6,451,200 won.

748
00:46:28,352 --> 00:46:29,887
Six million won?

749
00:46:29,954 --> 00:46:33,291
You look so scared, kid. Forget it.

750
00:46:33,357 --> 00:46:35,860
I'll call it even with this.

751
00:46:39,130 --> 00:46:40,865
How about another round?

752
00:46:40,931 --> 00:46:42,466
No, I don't want to.

753
00:46:42,533 --> 00:46:45,636
Should we get going now, then?

754
00:46:45,703 --> 00:46:48,239
-Get home safe.
-Hurry on home, sir.

755
00:46:48,306 --> 00:46:49,640
Get home safe.

756
00:46:52,710 --> 00:46:56,614
60,000 points? In Go-Stop, 60…

757
00:46:56,681 --> 00:46:57,815
How's that possible?

758
00:46:57,882 --> 00:46:59,750
Hey, how is that possible?

759
00:46:59,817 --> 00:47:01,585
Didn't I tell you not to play?

760
00:47:01,652 --> 00:47:02,887
All because of you…

761
00:47:02,953 --> 00:47:05,623
You're the bane of my life, seriously.

762
00:47:06,223 --> 00:47:09,360
That old man's a card hustler, 100%.

763
00:47:21,739 --> 00:47:24,208
Ugh, ramen again?

764
00:47:24,275 --> 00:47:26,777
When are you making me spaghetti?

765
00:47:26,844 --> 00:47:28,446
I said to make it yourself.

766
00:47:28,512 --> 00:47:31,349
So petty and stingy. No, thank you.

767
00:47:34,118 --> 00:47:37,488
Um, I'll give up on the spaghetti,

768
00:47:37,555 --> 00:47:39,590
so please do me one favor.

769
00:47:40,224 --> 00:47:43,327
-What favor?
-Just lend me a million won.

770
00:47:43,394 --> 00:47:45,496
I need to put plastic over the field,

771
00:47:45,563 --> 00:47:46,964
but I'm this much short.

772
00:47:47,031 --> 00:47:49,300
Oh, please. Forget it.

773
00:47:49,367 --> 00:47:51,535
How could I trust you with a loan?

774
00:47:52,536 --> 00:47:55,606
Come on, just lend it to me.
I swear I'll pay you back.

775
00:47:55,673 --> 00:47:57,875
Oh, please. No, thank you.

776
00:47:57,942 --> 00:47:59,577
Besides, why borrow from me?

777
00:47:59,643 --> 00:48:02,513
Borrow it from that big shot,
Yu-na or Yuzu.

778
00:48:02,580 --> 00:48:04,615
Why are you bringing up Yu-na?

779
00:48:04,682 --> 00:48:06,784
Gosh, whenever I bring up Yu-na,

780
00:48:06,851 --> 00:48:09,787
you tremble all over like crazy.

781
00:48:09,854 --> 00:48:12,690
Gosh, why? You like Yu-na that much?
That much?

782
00:48:12,757 --> 00:48:15,393
Look at Mr. True Love, Mr. Pure Love.

783
00:48:15,459 --> 00:48:17,361
Come on, knock it off.

784
00:48:17,428 --> 00:48:21,232
What is wrong with you?
Why are you like this with me lately?

785
00:48:21,298 --> 00:48:23,667
What's the reason?
Did I do something wrong?

786
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:25,002
There's no reason, okay?

787
00:48:25,069 --> 00:48:27,037
Then why are you always so annoyed?

788
00:48:27,104 --> 00:48:29,640
If I did something wrong, tell me.

789
00:48:29,707 --> 00:48:30,808
Oh, forget it!

790
00:48:30,875 --> 00:48:33,177
I don't want to talk to you, so stop.

791
00:48:33,244 --> 00:48:34,979
What?

792
00:48:36,514 --> 00:48:38,115
Fine.

793
00:48:38,182 --> 00:48:40,117
I won't speak to you from now on,

794
00:48:40,184 --> 00:48:43,053
so don't speak to me either, got it?

795
00:48:44,255 --> 00:48:46,390
Stuff your face with MSG, damn it.

796
00:49:24,261 --> 00:49:28,032
Do I have to pull weeds all day again?

797
00:49:28,098 --> 00:49:29,967
I'm sick to death of it.

798
00:49:30,968 --> 00:49:32,603
If only we had a million won.

799
00:49:32,670 --> 00:49:34,505
Any part-time jobs around here?

800
00:49:34,572 --> 00:49:37,675
Jeez, how could we make
a million won working part-time?

801
00:49:37,741 --> 00:49:40,077
This is so frustrating, seriously.

802
00:49:45,182 --> 00:49:47,351
What? Going to the field like that?

803
00:49:47,418 --> 00:49:48,819
I'm heading to Seoul.

804
00:49:48,886 --> 00:49:51,455
What? We have to pull weeds.
Where are you going?

805
00:49:51,522 --> 00:49:54,024
I have something I really need to do.

806
00:49:54,091 --> 00:49:56,327
Hey, bring me back an Americano then.

807
00:49:56,393 --> 00:49:58,095
I'm sick of instant coffee now.

808
00:49:58,162 --> 00:50:00,064
-Got new clothes?
-I had them, man.

809
00:50:00,130 --> 00:50:02,333
-Got it?
-I got it, you pest!

810
00:50:02,399 --> 00:50:03,968
Hey, guys, come in and eat.

811
00:50:04,034 --> 00:50:06,003
-Okay.

812
00:50:09,306 --> 00:50:11,075
Lee Min-gi, where are you going?

813
00:50:11,141 --> 00:50:12,877
Aren't you going to eat?

814
00:50:18,382 --> 00:50:20,284
-Good morning. You're up?
-Yes.

815
00:50:21,485 --> 00:50:24,021
Why is it just you two?
Where are the others?

816
00:50:24,088 --> 00:50:27,758
Han-cheol went to Seoul,
and Min-gi says he's not eating.

817
00:50:27,825 --> 00:50:30,427
-He had a big fight with Yun-hui.
-A big fight?

818
00:50:30,494 --> 00:50:32,630
Yun-hui, you fought with Min-gi again?

819
00:50:32,696 --> 00:50:35,599
We're not kids. We didn't fight.

820
00:50:35,666 --> 00:50:39,003
Just leave him alone.
Only he goes hungry if he doesn't eat.

821
00:50:39,069 --> 00:50:41,739
Anyway, I really don't like that guy.

822
00:50:42,573 --> 00:50:44,275
Sis, tell me if he bothers you.

823
00:50:44,341 --> 00:50:46,644
I won't let him off easily.

824
00:50:47,912 --> 00:50:51,515
Don't worry about that.
I'll protect her.

825
00:50:52,483 --> 00:50:53,851
Why would you protect her?

826
00:50:53,918 --> 00:50:55,986
Because I like her.

827
00:50:58,856 --> 00:51:01,292
What's this bullshit all of a sudden?

828
00:51:02,459 --> 00:51:03,527
It's true.

829
00:51:04,695 --> 00:51:08,232
Hyeok, I really like you too.

830
00:51:08,299 --> 00:51:11,268
But if you keep this up,
I'll really start to hate you.

831
00:51:11,335 --> 00:51:13,170
So let's just eat quietly, okay?

832
00:51:13,237 --> 00:51:16,173
Anyway, sometimes this guy
seems completely crazy.

833
00:51:16,240 --> 00:51:18,208
What are you doing during a meal?

834
00:51:18,275 --> 00:51:20,210
-Just eat.
-Seriously…

835
00:51:26,283 --> 00:51:27,918
Thank you.

836
00:51:29,486 --> 00:51:32,389
She promised my money ages ago
and still hasn't sent it?

837
00:51:32,456 --> 00:51:35,492
This is so cheap and petty,
I'm going there myself.

838
00:51:39,229 --> 00:51:42,433
While I'm up there,
I'll see how that jerk is doing too.

839
00:51:43,667 --> 00:51:48,005
GWANGJU, JEONJU, GANGNEUNG

840
00:52:57,174 --> 00:53:00,511
Jeez, that was so uncomfortable,
I thought I'd die.

841
00:53:01,679 --> 00:53:03,047
Su-yeon.

842
00:53:05,382 --> 00:53:09,253
Hello, Team Leader.
What brings you here?

843
00:53:09,319 --> 00:53:11,555
I'm heading out on a business trip.

844
00:53:11,622 --> 00:53:13,857
But what are you doing here, Su-yeon?

845
00:53:13,924 --> 00:53:16,326
Um… I'm just traveling…

846
00:53:18,429 --> 00:53:19,463
Traveling?

847
00:53:19,530 --> 00:53:22,266
You quit without a word,
and now you have it easy.

848
00:53:22,332 --> 00:53:25,502
Do you know how much
I'm working my ass off thanks to you?

849
00:53:25,569 --> 00:53:27,471
You need a sense of responsibility.

850
00:53:27,538 --> 00:53:30,708
This is why third-rate college grads
just don't cut it.

851
00:53:35,546 --> 00:53:39,183
Must've been hard on you without me.

852
00:53:40,050 --> 00:53:43,253
After all, you have to copy
and steal my designs again.

853
00:53:43,320 --> 00:53:45,289
No wonder it's hard on you.

854
00:53:45,889 --> 00:53:48,625
Copy you? What are you talking about?

855
00:53:48,692 --> 00:53:51,995
Do you really not remember?
Or are you just playing dumb?

856
00:53:52,062 --> 00:53:54,932
How can an elite overseas grad
have such a pea brain?

857
00:53:54,998 --> 00:53:57,134
How dare you talk to me like that?

858
00:53:57,201 --> 00:53:59,937
Su-yeon, how do you plan
to work in this industry?

859
00:54:00,971 --> 00:54:03,440
So I'm going to study abroad too.

860
00:54:03,507 --> 00:54:06,977
Then, like you all, I'll copy
third-rate college juniors' work

861
00:54:07,044 --> 00:54:10,781
and live on easy street.
So sit tight and wait for me.

862
00:54:10,848 --> 00:54:14,785
You're just talentless hacks
power-tripping on foreign degrees.

863
00:54:14,852 --> 00:54:17,321
I'm going to crush every one of you.

864
00:54:17,387 --> 00:54:19,022
Got that?

865
00:54:23,994 --> 00:54:25,195
Why are you staring?

866
00:54:25,929 --> 00:54:27,965
Do you have something to say?

867
00:54:28,031 --> 00:54:31,235
No, nothing. I'm so sorry.

868
00:54:31,301 --> 00:54:33,103
This industry is a small world.

869
00:54:33,170 --> 00:54:34,671
Everyone knows everyone.

870
00:54:34,738 --> 00:54:37,508
I let it go because I'm a nice person.

871
00:54:37,574 --> 00:54:39,476
But to survive in this industry,

872
00:54:39,543 --> 00:54:41,979
keep your head on straight.

873
00:54:50,053 --> 00:54:53,123
How much longer do we have
to keep pulling weeds? Jeez.

874
00:54:53,190 --> 00:54:56,527
Why do these stupid weeds
grow right back after we pull them?

875
00:54:57,094 --> 00:54:58,896
Let's stop this and ask Yun-hui

876
00:54:58,962 --> 00:55:00,464
for a loan again, okay?

877
00:55:00,531 --> 00:55:01,565
Forget it!

878
00:55:01,632 --> 00:55:04,001
I'm too proud to ever
borrow money from her.

879
00:55:04,067 --> 00:55:05,836
I don't know what happened,

880
00:55:05,903 --> 00:55:07,805
but just make up like grown adults.

881
00:55:07,871 --> 00:55:09,506
Shut up!

882
00:55:09,573 --> 00:55:11,241
Until she apologizes first,

883
00:55:11,308 --> 00:55:13,510
I'm never speaking to her again.

884
00:55:13,577 --> 00:55:16,446
Guys! Hey, guys!

885
00:55:16,513 --> 00:55:18,749
You guys said you needed money, right?

886
00:55:18,816 --> 00:55:21,185
That's right. Why?

887
00:55:21,251 --> 00:55:24,121
-Would you like a side gig?
-A side gig? What kind?

888
00:55:24,188 --> 00:55:27,491
Today is my friend's grandmother's
70th birthday party.

889
00:55:28,058 --> 00:55:30,928
I hear that depending on how you do,

890
00:55:30,994 --> 00:55:32,629
you could make a million won.

891
00:55:33,797 --> 00:55:35,532
What? Really?

892
00:55:36,900 --> 00:55:38,535
-I'm in!

893
00:55:39,069 --> 00:55:42,172
But what do we do at a 70th birthday
to get a million won?

894
00:55:45,042 --> 00:55:49,479
MADAM KIM KKEUT-SUN'S
70TH BIRTHDAY BANQUET

895
00:56:13,737 --> 00:56:17,307
My goodness, where did
such pretty boys come from?

896
00:56:18,775 --> 00:56:21,011
Goodness, how cute. You're so cute!

897
00:56:21,078 --> 00:56:23,013
Okay, all right, all right.

898
00:56:25,148 --> 00:56:27,517
Here, crisp green 10,000-won bills!

899
00:56:31,088 --> 00:56:33,323
My, look how fair your skin is.

900
00:56:34,424 --> 00:56:37,060
Goodness me, aren't you a pretty one!

901
00:56:38,862 --> 00:56:40,497
Hey, Min-gi!

902
00:57:08,458 --> 00:57:10,060
PARK MUN-SAM

903
00:57:41,224 --> 00:57:42,859
I knew it.

904
00:57:42,926 --> 00:57:46,096
He can't be awake already
after such a big accident.

905
00:57:47,931 --> 00:57:49,599
Then…

906
00:57:50,901 --> 00:57:54,004
who on earth were those thugs
who came to the shop?

907
00:58:22,232 --> 00:58:23,767
Who are you guys?

908
00:58:23,834 --> 00:58:25,335
-Let's go.
-Who are you?

909
00:58:38,315 --> 00:58:41,318
Who are you?
What are you doing outside my room?

910
00:58:41,385 --> 00:58:44,454
What? Um, I…

911
00:58:44,521 --> 00:58:46,289
I got the wrong room.

912
00:58:46,356 --> 00:58:47,958
I'm sorry.

913
00:58:51,028 --> 00:58:53,463
She looks familiar.
Where have I seen her?

914
00:58:53,530 --> 00:58:57,000
Wait! Doesn't she look just like her?

915
00:58:58,535 --> 00:59:00,904
But her hair color's different.
It's not her.

916
00:59:00,971 --> 00:59:02,339
Hey, you idiot!

917
00:59:02,406 --> 00:59:04,174
This is a wig! A wig!

918
00:59:05,175 --> 00:59:06,476
Hey, stop right there!

919
00:59:06,543 --> 00:59:08,178
-Hey!

920
00:59:09,446 --> 00:59:10,514
Hey, stop!

921
00:59:10,580 --> 00:59:12,549
-Hey!
-Get her!

922
00:59:15,619 --> 00:59:17,287
Hey, the stairs! Go!

923
00:59:19,189 --> 00:59:20,624
MEDICATION DOSAGE GUIDE

924
00:59:20,690 --> 00:59:22,959
Painkillers can only do so much.

925
00:59:23,026 --> 00:59:26,029
Why don't you just get admitted now?

926
00:59:34,871 --> 00:59:37,541
Right, he told me to buy coffee.

927
00:59:49,319 --> 00:59:50,387
She's gone!

928
00:59:50,454 --> 00:59:52,489
She can't have escaped yet. Find her!

929
00:59:52,556 --> 00:59:53,623
Damn it!

930
00:59:56,159 --> 01:00:00,063
Where's the Americano… Here it is.

931
01:00:13,610 --> 01:00:15,545
Um, excuse me, Han-cheol.

932
01:00:15,612 --> 01:00:16,780
Please help me.

933
01:00:16,847 --> 01:00:18,915
You said not to act like I know you.

934
01:00:18,982 --> 01:00:21,685
You said you'd bash my head in
if I talked to you.

935
01:00:22,219 --> 01:00:23,687
I was just so angry…

936
01:00:23,753 --> 01:00:26,323
I'm sorry. I went too far.

937
01:00:30,894 --> 01:00:33,163
Then can I act like I know you now?

938
01:00:34,064 --> 01:00:37,934
Okay, fine, so just help me, please?

939
01:00:38,001 --> 01:00:39,769
Okay! What can I do for you?

940
01:00:39,836 --> 01:00:42,739
Just say the word.
I'll do anything. What is it?

941
01:01:06,296 --> 01:01:08,431
Excuse me, you dropped this.

942
01:01:08,498 --> 01:01:10,066
I threw it away.

943
01:01:10,133 --> 01:01:13,003
It's still full.
Why throw it away? What a waste.

944
01:01:13,069 --> 01:01:14,137
Just because.

945
01:01:14,204 --> 01:01:16,540
Why? Can't I throw it away?

946
01:01:17,674 --> 01:01:19,009
Hold on.

947
01:01:33,223 --> 01:01:34,891
Then…

948
01:01:38,295 --> 01:01:40,163
I can keep this, right?

949
01:01:40,230 --> 01:01:43,567
Yes, yes!

950
01:01:43,633 --> 01:01:46,536
Please, have it. Well, then…

951
01:01:57,581 --> 01:01:59,382
Su-yeon, run away!

952
01:02:01,885 --> 01:02:03,853
No, no!

953
01:02:04,654 --> 01:02:06,923
-Hey!
-No, no!

954
01:02:06,990 --> 01:02:09,793
-What is this?
-Su-yeon, run!

955
01:02:09,859 --> 01:02:11,628
Su-yeon!
